# Grothendieck tribute — Part 52: arrow form of the topology generated by a coverage

Alexandre Grothendieck (1928-2014).

Extension Phase 5 (#2159, EPIC #1646).

Parts 1-51 established the fundamentals: categories, sieves, topologies,
lattice laws, pullback identities, sheaf bases, covering closure,
calibration, subcanonicity, dense topologies, sheaves, internal hom,
Čech cohomology, Mayer-Vietoris limit, Kan extensions, adjunctions,
monads, equivalences, monoidal categories, the Grothendieck construction,
direct/exceptional image, the arrow form of the covering, the coherence
laws of the pullback pseudo-functor, the indexed lattice laws, the arrow
form of dense, extremal, pushforward-pullback adjunction, bind,
pretopology-generated, induced-topology, cover-preserving functors and
the composition laws of these functors.

This part applies the "arrow form" leitmotiv to the **topology generated
by a coverage** (`Coverage.toGrothendieck`). Mathlib provides at the point
level `Coverage.mem_toGrothendieck`:
`S ∈ K.toGrothendieck X ↔ Saturate K X S`, but **no law connects it to the
arrow form** `J.Covers`. We fill the gap with five proper theorems:

  - `covers_iff_toGrothendieck` (central): for `J := K.toGrothendieck`,
    `J.Covers S f ↔ Saturate K Y (S.pullback f)` — direct bridge between
    the arrow form and the inductive extension `Saturate`, via
    `covers_iff` and `Coverage.mem_toGrothendieck`. This is the **natural
    law** connecting the covering in the sense of Grothendieck and the
    covering in the sense of Cover (1957).
  - `covers_toGrothendieck_of_of` (particular case): if `R ∈ K X` is a
    covering family, then the sieve it generates covers the identity:
    `K.toGrothendieck.Covers (Sieve.generate R) (𝟙 X)` — the forward
    direction of `Saturate.of`.
  - `covers_toGrothendieck_of_top` (particular case): the trivial cover
    `⊤` covers any arrow: `K.toGrothendieck.Covers ⊤ f`. Fall-out of the
    constructor `Saturate.top` via `covers_iff` and `mem_toGrothendieck`.
  - `covers_of_mem_toGrothendieck` (passage via `Sieve.generate`): if
    `R` is a covering family for K, then
    `K.toGrothendieck.Covers (Sieve.generate R) f` — for any arrow
    `f : Y ⟶ X`, the cover descends one notch via pullback stability
    (`Saturate.pullback`) and pullback monotonicity.
  - `covers_iff_pullback_toGrothendieck` (particular case on identity):
    `K.toGrothendieck.Covers S (𝟙 X) ↔ S ∈ K.toGrothendieck X` — the
    point-level fall-out, direct specialization of `covers_iff_covers_id`
    (Part 35) to the case `J := K.toGrothendieck`. The proof of
    `covers_iff_covers_id` is inlined to make this module self-sufficient
    (Part 35 is not necessarily on `main` at the date of this PR).

Each proof is a **real tactical proof** (DEEP vein): Mathlib axioms
(`GrothendieckTopology.covers_iff`, `Coverage.mem_toGrothendieck`,
`Coverage.Saturate.pullback`, `Coverage.Saturate.top`, `Coverage.Saturate.of`,
`Sieve.pullback_id`, `Sieve.pullback_monotone`, `Sieve.generate_sieve`) plus
the definition `Coverage.toGrothendieck`. No proof is a re-export or an
unfold.

EPIC #1646, Phase 5 (#2159). All `sorry`s eliminated at creation.

